s" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie5d1e2c5182d9a1cf1b9ae1b93eb3bc9955eb92b" commit="48c36a1220a411fe17295fb7176be5bb41379a88" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dmaengine: qcom: bam_dma: clear BAM interrupt only if it is raised  Currently we write BAM_IRQ_CLR register with zero even when no BAM_IRQ occured. This write has some bad side effects when the BAM instance is for the crypto engine. In case of crypto engine some of the BAM registers are xPU protected and they cannot be controlled by the driver.      BUG=chrome-os-partner:52995     TEST=none  Signed-off-by: Stanimir Varbanov &lt;stanimir.varbanov@linaro.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andy Gross &lt;andy.gross@linaro.org&gt; Tested-by: Pramod Gurav &lt;gpramod@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul &lt;vinod.koul@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit f89117c0f54c235c149d31174d1dd855e04765b8)  Change-Id: Ie5d1e2c5182d9a1cf1b9ae1b93eb3bc9955eb92b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342508 Commit-Ready: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Tested-by: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthew McClintock &lt;mmcclint@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342508" owner_email="ssambang@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/08/342508/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I9b7a627bb9d301d2ab7638f04b3b253e8de70578" commit="0347eb60360715dd746e1b4a87e50e40a6f53062" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dmaengine: qcom: bam_dma: add controlled-remotely dt property  Some of the peripherals has bam which is controlled by remote processor, thus the bam dma driver must avoid register writes which initialise bam hw block. Those registers are protected from xPU block and any writes to them will lead to secure violation and system reboot.  Adding the contolled_remotely flag in bam driver to avoid not permitted register writes in bam_init function.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52995 TEST=none  Signed-off-by: Stanimir Varbanov &lt;stanimir.varbanov@linaro.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andy Gross &lt;andy.gross@linaro.org&gt; Tested-by: Pramod Gurav &lt;gpramod@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul &lt;vinod.koul@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5172c9eb89d4ea41f86ff91b15b2b0dc75ded869)  Change-Id: I9b7a627bb9d301d2ab7638f04b3b253e8de70578 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342509 Commit-Ready: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Tested-by: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthew McClintock &lt;mmcclint@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342509" owner_email="ssambang@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/09/342509/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I84327b018fba3e019176f3622dc411e04f015055" commit="51fdc209d0a1440f06e6bb555e7863c7e868d1e8" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dmaengine: qcom: bam_dma: use correct pipe FIFO size  The pipe fifo size register must instruct the bam hw how many hw descriptors can be pushed to fifo. Currently we instruct the hw with 32KBytes but wrap the tail in bam_start_dma in BAM_P_EVNT_REG on 4095 i.e. 32760. This leads to stalled transactions when the tail wraps.  Fix this by use the correct fifo size in BAM_P_FIFO_SIZES register i.e. 32K - 8.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52995 TEST=Tested I2C and SPI with BAM Mode  Signed-off-by: Stanimir Varbanov &lt;stanimir.varbanov@linaro.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul &lt;vinod.koul@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 2a663ed9fe88cb237d72ce869aeadbbf119ad8e4)  Change-Id: I84327b018fba3e019176f3622dc411e04f015055 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342570 Commit-Ready: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Tested-by: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthew McClintock &lt;mmcclint@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342570" owner_email="ssambang@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/70/342570/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icf0b06652a680d152fb52ab1e884f93376ae5691" commit="4682d2976b67a707d6e8530b89e54b9be2c5867e" commit_message="Check /sys/dev/block/&lt;major&gt;:&lt;minor&gt;/queue/rotational first  then check with &lt;major&gt;:&lt;minor_with_mask&gt; if the first one fails. The original code always used 0 as a minor device number, but it didn't behave correctly when tracing sdb, loop1, etc.  BUG=b:25115863 BUG=b:25598659 TEST=ureadahead can trace files on a loop-mounted squashfs image TEST=the main pack file for / is still valid.  'ureadahead --dump / | grep ssd' returns 'for ssd'  Change-Id: Icf0b06652a680d152fb52ab1e884f93376ae5691 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341670 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="341670" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/70/341670/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic3745ebb145a9976a295e55744756017628989ba" commit="83c495e4280d7cc